    rdfs:label "shigley10-es-0033" ;
    ev:blockIdentifier "shigley10/p405/b2" ;
    ev:boundingBox "238.5,455.95,589.03,647.11" ;
    ev:extractedText "The square key, shown in Fig. 7–16a, is also available in rectangular sizes. Standard sizes of these, together with the range of applicable shaft diameters, are listed in Table 7–6. The shaft diameter determines standard sizes for width, height, and key depth. The designer chooses an appropriate key length to carry the torsional load. Failure of the key can be by direct shear, or by bearing stress. Example 7–6 demonstrates the process to size the length of a key. The maximum …"@en ;
