shigley10:es-0037 a ev:EvidenceSpan ;
    rdfs:label "shigley10-es-0037" ;
    ev:blockIdentifier "shigley10/p406/b1" ;
    ev:boundingBox "196.5,374.75,547.03,650.65" ;
    ev:extractedText "The gib-head key, in Fig. 7–17a, is tapered so that, when firmly driven, it acts to prevent relative axial motion. This also gives the advantage that the hub position can be adjusted for the best axial location. The head makes removal possible without access to the other end, but the projection may be hazardous. The Woodruff key, shown in Fig. 7–17b, is of general usefulness, especially when a wheel is to be positioned against a shaft shoulder, since the keyslot need not be …"@en ;
    ev:extractionConfidence 0.95 ;
